<title>NETHERLANDS: UBBINK IN THE RED AFTER ONE-OFF CHARGE.</title>
<headline>UBBINK IN THE RED AFTER ONE-OFF CHARGE.</headline>
<dateline>DOESBURG, Netherlands 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit from ordinary ops     0.8  vs   4.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary charge		 3.6  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Net loss after extraordinaries   2.8  vs   4.0 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover			     173    vs 172</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  nil  vs   2.10</p>
<p>    Cashflow per share (guilders)    6.94 vs  16.50</p>
<p>NOTE - Building materials trader Ubbink NV said in January</p>
<p>it expected a 1996 total loss of about three million guilders</p>
<p>because of reorganisation charges.</p>
</text>
